{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":72003155,"ns":0,"title":"Beta-model","extract":"In model theory, a mathematical discipline, a β-model (from the French \"bon ordre\", well-ordering) is a model that is correct about statements of the form \"X is well-ordered\". The term was introduced by Mostowski (1959) as a strengthening of the notion of ω-model.","description":"Class of \"well-behaved\" models in set theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}